@startuml import-sequence
title CSV import: upload, review, durable rows and derived views

!theme plain
hide footbox
skinparam participantPadding 15
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor User
participant "ImportPage / ImportReviewPage\nlib/api/imports.ts" as Frontend
participant "routes/importRoutes.js" as Route
participant "importPipeline\nindex.js + stage / validate / match / commit" as Pipeline
database "PostgreSQL\nbatches, staging rows, canonical ledger" as DB
participant "Post-commit services" as Derived

group 1. Prepare the uploaded rows
  User -> Frontend : Upload CSV and choose adapter
  Frontend -> Route : POST /api/import/csv/stream\nMultipart CSV + bank_name
  Route -> Pipeline : runImportPipeline(filePath, adapterName, onProgress)
  Pipeline -> DB : createBatch() and stageBatch()\nStore parsed rows with source metadata
  Pipeline -> Pipeline : validateBatch()\nRequired fields + source/occurrence identity
  Pipeline -> DB : Mark validated or error rows; persist fingerprints
  Pipeline -> Pipeline : matchBatch()\nPatterns, exact/fuzzy, then new recipients
  Pipeline -> DB : Resolve / upsert recipients;\nrecord match source and similarity
  Pipeline --> Route : Phase progress
  Route --> Frontend : Server-Sent Events progress
end

alt Pattern, fuzzy, new or unresolved recipient needs review
  Pipeline -> DB : Set awaiting_review
  Pipeline --> Route : requiresReview + batchId
  Route --> Frontend : review_required event
  Frontend --> User : Open review page
  Frontend -> Route : GET /api/import/batches/:id/preview
  Route -> DB : Read staged rows and match provenance
  DB --> Route : Grouped review data
  Route --> Frontend : Preview
  opt User corrects a recipient or category
    User -> Frontend : Choose replacement
    Frontend -> Route : POST .../rows/:rowId/override\nor .../rows/:rowId/category-override
    Route -> DB : Validate IDs and update matched staging row
    Route --> Frontend : Applied override
  end
  User -> Frontend : Commit reviewed batch
  Frontend -> Route : POST /api/import/batches/:id/commit
  Route -> Pipeline : commitImport(batchId)
else All eligible recipient matches are exact
  Pipeline -> Pipeline : commitImport(batchId)
end

group 2. Write canonical transactions
  Pipeline -> DB : Read matched rows; apply overrides;\nmark unresolved recipients as errors
  loop At most 1,000 rows per write transaction
    Pipeline -> DB : Resolve accounts; probe fingerprint / legacy identity
    Pipeline -> DB : Insert rows with savepoints + provenance;\nretain committed / duplicate / error staging status
    DB --> Pipeline : Committed chunk outcomes
    Pipeline -> DB : Checkpoint batch counters
  end
end

group 3. Reconcile after durable writes
  Pipeline -> Derived : autoLinkTransactions(insertedRows)
  Derived -> DB : Link unambiguous planned-payment matches
  Pipeline -> DB : Mark batch complete
  Pipeline -> Derived : reconcileTransfers() across full ledger
  Derived -> DB : Record internal-transfer pairs
  Pipeline -> Derived : Clear forecast caches if imported > 0;\nscheduleMaterializedViewRefresh()
  Pipeline --> Route : Imported / duplicate / error / auto-linked counts
  Route --> Frontend : complete event (auto path)\nor JSON result (review commit)
  Frontend --> User : Show summary
  Derived ->> DB : Refresh materialized views asynchronously
end

note over Pipeline, DB
  Source hashes preserve provenance; occurrence fingerprints identify rows.
  A failed later chunk does not undo earlier committed chunks.
  Planned matching and transfer reconciliation failures are non-fatal.
end note

note over Frontend, Route
  Non-streaming POST /api/import/csv is also supported:
  201 for committed counts; 202 for review-required batches.
end note

legend bottom
  Sources: lib/api/imports.ts; routes/importRoutes.js;
  services/importPipeline/; repositories/importBatchRepository.js;
  services/plannedMatchService.js; services/transferReconciliationService.js.
endlegend

@enduml
